{% set verb = {
  "Active":   "is now being worked on",
  "Committed":"is now committed for an upcoming milestone",
  "Resolved": "has been resolved internally",
  "Closed":   "has been closed",
  "Removed":  "was removed from our backlog",
  "Cut":      "was cut from the current scope"
} %}
Hi @{{ author }} — quick update on this one.

Our internal tracker for this issue {{ verb.get(new_state, "moved to **" ~ new_state ~ "**") }}.

{% if new_state in ["Resolved", "Closed"] -%}
If you're able to verify the fix on a recent Windows Admin Center build, please let us know
whether it works for you. If you still see the issue, comment here and we'll re-open the
investigation.
{%- elif new_state in ["Active", "Committed"] -%}
We'll post another update when there's more to share.
{%- else -%}
We wanted to keep you in the loop.
{%- endif %}

— The Windows Admin Center team

<!-- ado-state-update: {{ new_state }} from {{ previous_state or "unknown" }} -->
